      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MARKDKBERRY dot com\n\n## ISSUES \n\n1. \"For the Wan 2.2 5B (Hybrid) model, camera wobble or \"jerky\" motion is a common issue, often exacerbated by the use of Turbo or Lightning acceleration Loras, which are known to cause color shifting and increased camera instability\"\n   - try lowering shift to 2 (was 8) (ModelSampling3d node)\n   - Use the word \"shot\" instead (e.g., \"A static tripod shot\") (Out of everything I tried this worked best but had other issues like confetti)\n\n---\n\n2. NAG kept crapping out randomly sometimes after reboot with \"!! Exception during processing !!! mat1 and mat2 must have the same dtype, but got Half and Float \" error. \n\n- I think something NAG needed was somehow staying in cache somewhere from other workflows. I dont know. was weird.\n \n- Solution for me was to set weight_dtype in model node to fp8_e4m3fn (even thought its of little use on a 30xx card IIRC) instead of default.  "
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
